    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0529" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/5739: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Vice Consul at
                        Barcelona</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Flood</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-18T17:00:00-04:00">June 18, 1937—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of June 16, 3 p.m., in regard to the S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ciudad Barcelona</hi>. From the information in possession of the
                    Department, it would appear to be extremely unlikely that any airplane engines
                    of American manufacture were on the ship and almost inconceivable that there
                    could have been 800. Telegraph any further information which you may receive in
                    regard to this matter.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d479-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d479-f1" n="77" xml:id="d479-f1-content">
                <p>In his despatch No. 369, July 2, the Vice Consul at Barcelona reported that in
                    attempting to confirm, or disprove, the information contained in his telegram of
                    June 16, 3 p.m., to the Secretary of State, he had exhausted every available
                    source of information without reaching a solution (852.00/6016).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
